   "source": [
    "## 1. Analytical definitions\n",
    "\n",
    "The approved sign convention is:\n",
    "\n",
    "- Variance = Actual ? Budget\n",
    "- Variance percentage = (Actual ? Budget) / Budget ? 100\n",
    "- Positive variance indicates overspend.\n",
    "- Negative variance indicates underspend.\n",
    "- Zero variance indicates on-budget performance.\n",
    "\n",
    "Budget and Actual are the only measures used in variance calculations. Committed and Forecast remain separate contextual measures and are not added to either amount.\n",
    "\n",
    "Group percentages are calculated from group-level Budget and Actual totals, not by averaging individual percentages."
   ]
  },
